{"ts": 1789771447.668845, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Submitted: long feature 11 + long feature 14, predicted OOS Sharpe 1.15 \u00b1 0.33\n\n**How I got there**\n\nI scanned all 40 features individually. With n=5000 days (~20 years), the standard error on an in-sample Sharpe is ~0.22, which set the bar for what counts as evidence. Two features cleared it decisively: **11 (0.969)** and **14 (0.894)**, both ~4\u03c3. A middle tier (13, 24, 28, 39 at 0.29\u20130.47) sat at only 1\u20132\u03c3 \u2014 indistinguishable from noise once you account for having looked at 40 candidates.\n\nCombining the two strong features gave **1.318**, a real diversification gain over either alone, which is what you expect from two genuinely independent signals. Sign checks confirmed directionality: flipping either leg collapsed the Sharpe to ~0.055.\n\n**Why I stopped at two features instead of using the allowed three**\n\nEvery third feature I tried landed between 1.15 and 1.37 against the 1.318 baseline \u2014 the third slot did nothing systematic. The best candidate (13) added just +0.048, which is noise, and I'd selected it as the max over ~10 tries, so even that small edge is upward-biased by construction. Contrast this with the real thing: adding feature 14 to 11 moved the Sharpe by +0.35. A genuine third signal announces itself; this one didn't. Adding it would also dilute the two good legs from 1/2 to 1/3 weight each, so the expected OOS effect is roughly zero or negative.\n\n**On the prediction**\n\nI forecast 1.15 rather than the observed 1.318 because features 11 and 14 were themselves the winners of a 40-feature search \u2014 some of that in-sample number is selection luck, though their 4\u03c3 strength means the bias is modest. The SD of 0.33 reflects sampling error plus the risk that correlation structure or regime shifts differently out of sample.\n\nOne housekeeping note: several claude.ai MCP connectors reported needing authorization and can't be used in a non-interactive session. They were irrelevant here \u2014 this task only required `evaluate` and `submit` \u2014 but if you want them available later, they'd need to be authorized through your claude.ai connector settings, or via `claude mcp` / `/mcp` in an interactive session."}
